      </table></ix:nonNumeric></div><p style="margin-left:13.133%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:12pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:11pt;font-family:Times New Roman;min-width:fit-content;">Sensitivity analysis</span></p><p style="margin-left:13.133%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:12pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:11pt;font-family:Times New Roman;min-width:fit-content;">The Company is mainly exposed to the Singapore Dollar.</span></p><p style="margin-left:13.133%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:12pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:11pt;font-family:Times New Roman;min-width:fit-content;">The following table details the Company&#8217;s sensitivity to a </span><span style="font-size:11pt;font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_aaeb52c0-0ad8-480a-9f7f-e2d1e99ab400" contextRef="C_17c02880-b904-4701-8d5a-94e7274d281d" name="asln:PercentageOfDecreaseOnExchangeRateOfForeignCurrency" unitRef="U_pure" scale="-2" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">5</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:11pt;font-family:Times New Roman;min-width:fit-content;">% decrease in the U.S. dollar against the relevant foreign currency. The rate of </span><span style="font-size:11pt;font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_2a422ded-1cfe-425f-bd89-b974e3e2d47e" contextRef="C_17c02880-b904-4701-8d5a-94e7274d281d" name="asln:SensitivityAnalysisRate" unitRef="U_pure" scale="-2" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">5</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:11pt;font-family:Times New Roman;min-width:fit-content;">% is the sensitivity rate used when reporting foreign currency risk internally to key management personnel and represents management&#8217;s assessment of the reasonably possible change in foreign exchange rates. The sensitivity analysis includes only outstanding foreign currency denominated monetary items. A negative number below indicates an increase in pre-tax loss where the U.S. dollar weakens </span><span style="font-size:11pt;font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_2de5bc3d-1e71-4913-8969-c3a8cc8b6a68" contextRef="C_17c02880-b904-4701-8d5a-94e7274d281d" name="asln:PercentageOfDecreaseOnExchangeRateOfForeignCurrency" unitRef="U_pure" scale="-2" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">5</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:11pt;font-family:Times New Roman;min-width:fit-content;">% against the relevant currency. For a </span><span style="font-size:11pt;font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_1f90c1ea-27d9-44c9-851e-0f8d25e17c56" contextRef="C_17c02880-b904-4701-8d5a-94e7274d281d" name="asln:PercentageOfIncreaseOnExchangeRateOfForeignCurrency" unitRef="U_pure" scale="-2" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">5</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:11pt;font-family:Times New Roman;min-width:fit-content;">% strengthening of the U.S. dollar against the relevant currency, there would be an equal and opposite impact on pre-tax loss.</span></p><p style="margin-left:13.133%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;">&#160;</p><div style="font-size:12pt;font-family:Times New Roman;"><ix:nonNumeric id="F_88d03874-e166-497d-a798-5151de771c9b" contextRef="C_94db9b97-c113-414e-9ce4-7ac2413f8d3f" name="ifrs-full:SensitivityAnalysisForEachTypeOfMarketRisk" escape="true">
